{"type":"standard","title":"Mario Díaz-Balart","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mario Díaz-Balart</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q767270","titles":{"canonical":"Mario_Díaz-Balart","normalized":"Mario Díaz-Balart","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Mario Díaz-Balart</span></span>"},"pageid":411276,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart_official_photo.jpg/330px-Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart_official_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":496},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/04/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart_official_photo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":2795,"height":4200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1375210882","tid":"696984e6-b1d1-11f1-b223-c888b95accb8","timestamp":"2026-09-16T13:20:40Z","description":"American politician (born 1961)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Mario_D%C3%ADaz-Balart"}},"extract":"Mario Rafael Díaz-Balart y Caballero is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 26th congressional district. A member of the Republican Party, he was elected in 2002, and his district includes much of northwestern Miami-Dade County, including Hialeah, and much of the northern portion of the Everglades.","extract_html":"<p><b>Mario Rafael Díaz-Balart y Caballero</b> is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for Florida's 26th congressional district. A member of the Republican Party, he was elected in 2002, and his district includes much of northwestern Miami-Dade County, including Hialeah, and much of the northern portion of the Everglades.</p>"}